# Apple iOS (SwiftUI)

**Intent:** Native iOS implementation with SwiftUI — cross-surface product and accessibility policy stays in `universal-product.mdc` §2a (not duplicated here).

## Project structure **[core]**

Canonical layout under `Sources/`:

```
Sources/
  App/           # @main entry, app delegate/scene
  Views/         # SwiftUI screens and components
  ViewModels/    # @Observable / ObservableObject state
  Services/      # networking, persistence, platform APIs
  Models/        # domain types
  Resources/     # assets, Localizable.strings
Tests/           # unit + UI tests (parallel to Sources)
```

- Feature subpackages by layer or vertical slice when the app grows.
- View models that touch UI: mark **`@MainActor`**; keep networking off the main actor.

## UI & layout **[core]**

Align with `universal-product.mdc` §1b (Dieter Rams): prefer **system-native** over custom chrome — SF Symbols and standard controls are the digital equivalent of Rams’ restrained industrial forms.

- Prefer **native SwiftUI** controls, **SF Symbols**, and system materials for a consistent iOS look.
- **VStack, HStack, ZStack, Spacer, padding** for layout; **LazyVGrid / LazyHGrid** for grids; **GeometryReader** only when necessary.
- **`NavigationStack`** with typed routes (or coordinator) for deep links and back-stack clarity.
- **Gestures** and light **haptics** on primary actions; clear navigation hierarchy.
- Support **Dynamic Type**, **safe areas**, and **light/dark** appearance.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` for non-essential animation.

## Accessibility **[core]**

- Accessibility labels and hints on custom controls.
- VoiceOver smoke test on the primary user flow before release.
- Sufficient contrast; do not rely on color alone for state.

## Testing & release **[core]**

- Test on **minimum supported iOS** and latest iOS.
- XCTest for logic; XCUITest or SwiftUI Preview-driven checks where valuable.
- Align with **Apple Human Interface Guidelines** for platform conventions.

## What this rule does not cover

- Android / Jetpack Compose — see community rules or `universal-product.mdc` §2a for shared policy
- Web CSS layout → `website-building.mdc`
- Game engine / WebView shells → `games-building.mdc` § Android/iOS shell tags
